    basic: "Use the Manni exchange wisely - discard weak cards and hope to draw trumps or high cards. In Nullo, get rid of high cards early by playing them when you can't win the trick.",
    intermediate: 'Card counting is essential. Track which high cards have been played, especially in Nullo where you want to avoid taking tricks. In Grand and suit contracts, estimate how many tricks you can realistically win.',
    advanced: 'Contract selection strategy: Choose Grand when you have balanced high cards across suits. Choose a suit contract when you have length and strength in that suit. Choose Nullo when you have low cards and short suits. The exchange decision: Sometimes keeping a moderately strong hand is better than risking the Manni.',
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "In Nullo, leading low cards in long suits often forces opponents to win tricks they don't want",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Remember that in the 3-player game, there are only 16 tricks total',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'Track which Aces and Kings have been played - they determine who will win subsequent tricks',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'In suit contracts, voiding yourself in a weak suit lets you trump when that suit is led',
      },
